## Observed (public API, merged Core d21e5308b6 = D-090 + D-B112)
Repro `scratchpad/fix-dotnet-zoneworld-g4-and-teardown-outcomes/public-api-repro/repro.cpp` (main tree; read-only for you — copy it):
two TCP ROUTER sockets with RIDs, source submits a 5 s REQUEST that the target has received; then
- case 1 `zlink_close(target)` → completion `request_result=109` (NOT_CONNECTED) after 1 ms — correct (D-090).
- case 2 `zlink_disconnect(source, endpoint)` → `request_result=109` after 1 ms — **wrong**: the spec row for explicit removal is `ZLINK_REQUEST_NOT_FOUND`
  (102, `ENOENT`). On the previous Core (pre-D-090) the same case stayed pending until TIMED_OUT (101), so the NOT_FOUND path never fired for
  logical-RID requests at all.
Pointer from the previous job: `core/src/api/socket/socket_request_reply_pending_api.cpp:161-185` — the endpoint pending matcher selects only
`logical_rid.empty()` requests (DEALER-style correlation), so ROUTER requests addressed by logical RID are skipped by the explicit-removal
completion; `socket_base_endpoint.cpp:1009-1034` (endpoint removal per-RID follow-up only ends blocking send waits). Then the pipe terminates
and `pipe_peer_terminated()` (D-090) completes it NOT_CONNECTED.

